    {
      "name": "Setup & Utilities",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Setup Instructions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://example.com",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "example.com"
              ]
            },
            "description": "# Postman Setup Instructions\n\n## 1. Import Environment Variables\nCreate a new environment with these variables:\n- `base_url`: http://localhost:8080 (or your server URL)\n- `token`: Your JWT bearer token (get from login)\n- `userId`: User ID to test with (existing user)\n- `doctorId`: Doctor ID (set after creating a doctor)\n- `patientId`: Patient ID (set after creating a patient)\n- `phoneNumber`: Phone number for patient search\n\n## 2. Get JWT Token\n1. First, register/login a user with ADMIN role\n2. Copy the token from response\n3. Paste into the `token` variable in Postman environment\n\n## 3. Test Flow\n1. **Create Doctor**: Use an existing userId\n2. Copy returned doctorId and set in environment\n3. **Create Patient**: Use an existing userId\n4. Copy returned patientId and set in environment\n5. Run other endpoints using the IDs\n\n## 4. Required User Roles\n- `ADMIN`: Full access to create/delete/update\n- `DOCTOR`: Can view patients\n- `PATIENT`: Can view own profile\n\n## 5. Expected Status Codes\n- 201: Created\n- 200: OK\n- 204: No Content (delete)\n- 400: Bad Request (validation error)\n- 404: Not Found\n- 403: Forbidden (insufficient role)\n\n## 6. Common Test Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: Full Doctor Workflow\n1. Create Doctor → Copy doctorId\n2. Get Doctor by ID\n3. Update Doctor\n4. Get by Specialization\n5. Update Status to ON_LEAVE\n6. Delete Doctor\n\n### Scenario 2: Full Patient Workflow\n1. Create Patient → Copy patientId\n2. Get Patient by ID\n3. Search by Name\n4. Get by Phone\n5. Update Patient\n6. Delete Patient\n\n### Scenario 3: Validation Testing\n1. Create Doctor with invalid times (end before start)\n2. Create Patient with invalid phone format\n3. Create Doctor with duplicate user_id\n4. Test missing required fields\n"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
